{"id": "en-da0610bd-0001", "text": "Let me refactor the login path in place, since it is the smallest possible change and the risk is contained. However, tracing the call sites I now think the session store is the real problem, so patching login would only hide it. We should fix the store first.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 109, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "strong-phrase", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 48, "topic_id": "da0610bd-login-session-store", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-da0610bd-0002", "text": "The obvious plan is to split the monolith into three services this sprint so each team owns its boundary. On second thought, that sequencing is wrong: the shared database is the real coupling, so splitting the services first would just move the pain around.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 106, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "strong-phrase", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 44, "topic_id": "da0610bd-monolith-split-order", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-da0610bd-0003", "text": "我一开始认为延迟主要来自缓存未命中，所以建议先扩容缓存集群。然而，把火焰图看了一遍之后，我发现真正的瓶颈其实是数据库连接池的排队，扩容缓存并不能解决这个问题。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 30, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "strong-phrase", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 79, "topic_id": "da0610bd-cache-performance", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-da0610bd-0004", "text": "最初我判断这个偶发失败是测试环境的网络抖动造成的，建议重跑几次观察。话说回来，我仔细看了失败日志，时间点每次都卡在同一个事务提交后的两毫秒，这不像是网络问题，更像是本地时钟精度导致的竞态。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 34, "scenario": "debugging", "turn_type": "strong-phrase", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 94, "topic_id": "da0610bd-intermittent-test-flake", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-da0610bd-0005", "text": "The stack trace points at the serializer, so I would start by adding a null check there and re-running the failing case. Wait — the null is set upstream in the parser, so guarding the serializer would just mask the real defect. Let me follow the parser branch instead.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 121, "scenario": "debugging", "turn_type": "interjection", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 49, "topic_id": "da0610bd-null-pointer-trace", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-da0610bd-0006", "text": "For this recursion problem I would have students trace the factorial call tree first, because seeing the pattern makes the base case obvious. Hold on, that approach buries the bug: the real lesson is why a missing base case causes a stack overflow, so I should demonstrate that failure first.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 142, "scenario": "teaching", "turn_type": "interjection", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 50, "topic_id": "da0610bd-recursion-base-case", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-da0610bd-0007", "text": "分页接口我打算用游标方案，因为它在数据量大时更稳定，也方便前端做无限滚动。等等，我突然想起来我们的下游消费方还是按页码拉取的，改成游标会直接破坏他们的兼容性，这个方案行不通。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 37, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "interjection", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 87, "topic_id": "da0610bd-api-pagination", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-da0610bd-0008", "text": "我们把发布时间定在月底，这样能给测试留出充足的时间，也让市场团队有时间准备。等一下，月底正好赶上季度结算，运维会非常忙，这个时间点选得太糟糕了。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 38, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "interjection", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 72, "topic_id": "da0610bd-release-schedule", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-da0610bd-0009", "text": "Adding an automatic retry around the payment call is a clean fix and keeps the handler short. But it breaks idempotency: without an idempotency key the retry can double-charge the customer, so we cannot ship it as is.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 94, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "clausal-adversative", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 38, "topic_id": "da0610bd-retry-idempotency", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-da0610bd-0010", "text": "Creating an index on the status column looks like an easy win, and the query plan should improve immediately. Yet the column has only three distinct values, so the planner will likely ignore the index and we would pay the write cost for nothing.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 110, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "clausal-adversative", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 44, "topic_id": "da0610bd-index-cardinality", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-da0610bd-0011", "text": "在课堂上先用同步读取来解释文件 I/O 是可以的，学生理解起来直观。但这样会把并发概念完全藏起来，后面的异步章节反而更难讲，所以这个顺序需要调整。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 34, "scenario": "teaching", "turn_type": "clausal-adversative", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 71, "topic_id": "da0610bd-synchronous-reading", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-da0610bd-0012", "text": "把堆内存调大确实能立刻缓解这个频繁的 OOM，看起来是稳妥的止血办法。不过根因是事件监听器没有被移除，调大堆只会把崩溃往后拖几个小时，问题迟早还会回来。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 35, "scenario": "debugging", "turn_type": "clausal-adversative", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 75, "topic_id": "da0610bd-memory-leak-heap", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-da0610bd-0013", "text": "I said we should read the config file synchronously at startup, and that is wrong. Actually, it must be async, because this handler runs inside the event loop and a blocking read would stall every other connection.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 83, "scenario": "debugging", "turn_type": "self-correction", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 37, "topic_id": "da0610bd-sync-vs-async-read", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-da0610bd-0014", "text": "Earlier I estimated this migration at two weeks and told the team to plan around that. I need to correct myself: after mapping the foreign keys I realize it is closer to six weeks, so the estimate I gave was badly optimistic.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 87, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "self-correction", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 42, "topic_id": "da0610bd-deadline-estimate", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-da0610bd-0015", "text": "刚才我说这里捕获异常后直接返回默认值是合理的，因为能让调用方继续运行。其实我错了，这样做会把权限校验失败也吞掉，等于制造了一个安全漏洞，必须让异常继续向上抛出。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 35, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "self-correction", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 80, "topic_id": "da0610bd-error-swallowing", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-da0610bd-0016", "text": "我前面说样本量已经足够，可以下结论了，因为置信区间看起来很窄。我得收回这个判断：后来我发现数据里有大量重复样本被重复计数，真实的样本量远小于表面数字。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 31, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "self-correction", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 75, "topic_id": "da0610bd-sample-size-conclusion", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-da0610bd-0017", "text": "Writing through to the cache on every update seems fine, and the code stays simple. Then again, it does not: under a write-heavy workload every write blocks on the cache, and the latency we saved on reads we now pay back on writes.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 84, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "hedged-return", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 43, "topic_id": "da0610bd-cache-invalidation-cost", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-da0610bd-0018", "text": "Grading purely on the final answer looks fair and is quick to apply. That said, on reflection it is not fair at all, because it rewards lucky guesses and punishes students who reasoned correctly but slipped in arithmetic.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 69, "scenario": "teaching", "turn_type": "hedged-return", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 38, "topic_id": "da0610bd-grading-rubric", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-da0610bd-0019", "text": "把这块独立任务交给一个新同事来做，看起来挺合适，既能锻炼他也能减轻我的负担。话虽如此，仔细想想并不合适，因为他对这套构建系统完全不熟，前期沟通成本可能比我自己做完还高。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 38, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "hedged-return", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 84, "topic_id": "da0610bd-team-delegation", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-da0610bd-0020", "text": "先直接重跑一次 CI 看看能不能过，这个做法看起来省事又高效。不过再琢磨一下，这办法其实靠不住，因为失败是间歇性的，重跑通过只会掩盖真正的不稳定，必须去查日志。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 31, "scenario": "debugging", "turn_type": "hedged-return", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 78, "topic_id": "da0610bd-flaky-ci-rerun", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-da0610bd-0021", "text": "This refactoring approach is cleaner but it requires more upfront work, so the team should weigh the tradeoffs carefully before committing to either direction. Both options keep the same external behaviour, and the choice really comes down to how much review bandwidth we can afford this sprint.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 47, "topic_id": "da0610bd-neg-but-additive-1", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "but", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-da0610bd-0022", "text": "The streaming pipeline is the better fit for this workload. However, there is also a batch version available in the same repository if throughput matters more than latency, so either one is defensible depending on the target service level.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 39, "topic_id": "da0610bd-neg-however-aside-2", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "however", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-da0610bd-0023", "text": "The bug could come from a race in the worker pool but it could equally come from a stale cache entry, so we should gather more evidence before picking a suspect. Instrumenting both paths for one more cycle costs very little and keeps our options open.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "debugging", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 46, "topic_id": "da0610bd-neg-but-balanced-3", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "but", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-da0610bd-0024", "text": "We can ship the feature behind a flag this quarter. However, the mobile client will lag behind by one release, which is a normal rollout cost worth accepting, and the marketing team has already planned the launch around that.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 39, "topic_id": "da0610bd-neg-however-extra-4", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "however", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-da0610bd-0025", "text": "Recursion is elegant here but it is also harder for beginners to trace, and both of those facts are true at once, which is why this lesson pairs it with an iterative version so students can compare the two side by side.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "teaching", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 42, "topic_id": "da0610bd-neg-but-and-5", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "but", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-da0610bd-0026", "text": "The service is fast and the code is tidy, yet it still needs a load test before we trust it under production traffic, so that is the next item on the checklist. Everything so far supports shipping it once the load test is green.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 44, "topic_id": "da0610bd-neg-yet-listing-6", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "yet", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-da0610bd-0027", "text": "This clustering looks promising for the retention analysis. However, the dataset only covers a single quarter, so any seasonal effect is invisible for now, and we should note that limitation explicitly in the write-up.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 34, "topic_id": "da0610bd-neg-however-factual-7", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "however", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-da0610bd-0028", "text": "The stack trace is consistent with a null dereference but it is also consistent with an empty collection, so the two hypotheses still need a targeted test to separate them. For now I would keep both on the list rather than commit to one.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "debugging", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 44, "topic_id": "da0610bd-neg-but-adds-detail-8", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "but", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-da0610bd-0029", "text": "Before touching the shared counter, the worker must wait for the mutex to be released, otherwise the increment can be lost under concurrent load. This is a standard pattern and the code already documents it clearly.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 36, "topic_id": "da0610bd-neg-wait-for-lock-9", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "wait for", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-da0610bd-0030", "text": "After starting the migration, the operator should wait until the replica catches up before routing any read traffic to it, or queries will return stale rows. The runbook spells this out and the monitoring dashboard shows the lag.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "debugging", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 38, "topic_id": "da0610bd-neg-wait-until-10", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "wait until", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-da0610bd-0031", "text": "In this exercise the students have to wait for the build to finish before running the test suite, because the binary is produced as a side effect of compilation. That ordering is intentional and the worksheet explains why.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "teaching", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 38, "topic_id": "da0610bd-neg-wait-to-11", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "da0610bd-1b0f-4594-b8a4-05684632afda", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "wait for", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
